# {{PROJECT_NAME}}

This repository contains the analysis and manuscript for **{{PROJECT_NAME}}**.
It is organized so that a new collaborator can identify inputs, rerun the
analysis, inspect the manuscript source, and reproduce the journal handoff.

## Start here

1. Read this file and notes/active.md.
2. Put a provenance note in data/raw/README.md before adding data.
3. Add analysis in R/ in numbered execution order.
4. Run the analysis and write generated artifacts to output/results/,
   output/tables/, and output/figures/.
5. Write the manuscript in paper.qmd.
6. Run the manuscript helper with Rscript scripts/render-paper.R.

## Project map

| Location | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| data/raw/ | Original or received data. Document access and provenance. |
| data/processed/ | Reproducibly derived analysis data. |
| R/ | Numbered data, cleaning, estimation, and export scripts. |
| code/ | Non-R utilities, command-line tools, or supplementary code. |
| sandbox/ | Disposable exploration. Promote stable work into R/. |
| notes/active.md | Current tasks, decisions, questions, and handoffs. |
| notes/archive/ | Dated notes kept for project history. |
| output/results/ | Machine-readable model results and diagnostics. |
| output/tables/ | Tables used in the paper or supplement. |
| output/figures/ | Figures used in the paper or supplement. |
| output/manuscript/ | Quarto HTML, DOCX, and PDF renders. |
| paper.qmd | Single source of truth for the manuscript. |
| paper.tex | TeX copied from the latest PDF render for journal submission. |
| scripts/run-analysis.R | Runs the numbered R analysis scripts in order. |
| scripts/render-paper.R | Renders the manuscript in selected formats. |
| renv.lock | Package versions for reproducible R execution. |

## Rendering

Install Quarto and a LaTeX engine such as TinyTeX. Then run all formats:

~~~sh
Rscript scripts/run-analysis.R
Rscript scripts/render-paper.R
~~~

Or render selected formats:

~~~sh
Rscript scripts/render-paper.R --formats=pdf,docx
Rscript scripts/render-paper.R --formats=html
~~~

The helper runs Quarto from the project root. PDF rendering retains the
generated TeX and refreshes paper.tex. If the journal requires a specific
document class, bibliography style, or LaTeX package, update _quarto.yml
and the manuscript metadata before submission.

## Reproducibility

Run the following after changing dependencies:

~~~r
renv::snapshot()
paperrepo::check_paper_project()
~~~

For a clean handoff, clone this repository into a new directory, run
renv::restore(), execute the numbered scripts in R/, and render all
manuscript formats. Record any data-access restrictions in the data README
files and provide a synthetic or public substitute when raw data cannot be
redistributed.

